#ROOM
Vnum     15000
Name     The Shattered Road~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     What was once a grand processional road leading to the ruins of Kar'ethis
has been reclaimed by a dead landscape. Cracked black stone paving leads
north toward a silhouette of crumbled spires against a darkened sky. The
air here tastes of ozone and something older...something wrong. The ruins
loom ahead with a gravity that seems to tug at you even from this distance.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15001
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15001
Name     The Broken Gate~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The outer gate of Kar'ethis has long since collapsed, its massive stone
pillars toppled to either side of the road. Ancient Sith script runs along
the fallen stones, warning in no uncertain terms that death awaits all who
enter without the blessing of the dark side. The ruins proper begin to the
north and the approach road leads south.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15002
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15003
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 2 15001
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15002
Name     The Road of Subjugation~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The road widens here into what was once a ceremonial approach. Stone statues
of robed Sith line the path to the north, many broken but some still standing
in eerie silence. Their carved faces all share the same expression: absolute
contempt. The outer courtyard lies ahead and the broken gate is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15001
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 2 15002
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15003
Name     The Eastern Watch Post~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A crumbled guardhouse sits to the east of the broken gate. The roof has
long since caved in but the thick walls still stand. Old weapon racks line
one wall, empty now, and a narrow arrow slit still provides a view of the
approach road. A faded sigil on the floor marks this as a place where dark
side warriors once stood sentinel.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15001
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15004 1 15003
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15004
Name     The Western Watch Post~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A mirror to the eastern watch post, this crumbled structure sits west of the
gate. Unlike its counterpart it has not fully collapsed — a partial upper
floor remains accessible by a crumbling stone stair. From the upper position
the full sweep of the approach road is visible. The gate lies to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15001
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15004 1 15004
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15005
Name     The Waystone~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     An ancient waystone stands at a fork in the road leading to the ruins.
Carved from the same black stone as the ruins themselves it predates them
by an unknown margin. Sith script has been added to the original carvings
at a later date — warnings layered on top of older warnings. The road to
the ruins continues north and the approach road lies south.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15006
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 1 15005
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15006
Name     The Dead Plains~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A broad flat expanse of dead grey earth stretching south of the waystone.
Nothing grows here and nothing moves. The soil has been corrupted by dark
side energy seeping outward from the ruins over centuries. Even the wind
seems reluctant to cross this ground. The waystone is visible to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15007
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 1 15006
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15007
Name     The Ossuary Field~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Bones protrude from the dead earth here in scattered clusters — the remains
of those who came to the ruins and did not leave. Some appear to have simply
fallen where they stood, as though struck down at a distance. The density
of remains increases toward the ruins. The dead plains lie to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15006
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15003
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 2 15007
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15008
Name     The Forgotten Camp~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The remains of an old camp sit here on the western approach to the ruins.
Whoever set this up planned to stay for some time — the site is organised
and well-positioned. Whatever happened to the occupants is unclear. Their
equipment remains but they do not. The camp connects back toward the ruins
approach to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 1 15008
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15009
Name     The Scorched Ground~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A section of the approach ground that has been scorched black by some
ancient event. The scorch pattern radiates outward from a central point
in a way that suggests a single catastrophic release of energy. Whatever
caused this left no other trace. The approach road continues north toward
the broken gate and the dead plains lie to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15006
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 1 15009
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     15010
Name     The Outer Courtyard~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The outer courtyard of Kar'ethis stretches across a broad expanse of
dead stone. What was once an assembly ground for Sith rituals is now a
field of broken pillars and scattered debris. Dark stains mark the stone
in patterns that suggest the courtyard has witnessed unspeakable things.
Paths lead in all directions through the ruins and the approach road lies
to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15002
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15011
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 2 15010
Reset M 0 15004 1 15010
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15011
Name     The Altar of Binding~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A massive stone altar dominates this section of the courtyard, partially
sheltered by a remaining section of roof. Dark runes cover every surface of
the altar and the stone around it is permanently stained. Chains of black
metal hang from the altar corners. Whatever happened here was done many times
over many years. The courtyard lies to the south and a corridor leads north
into deeper ruins.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15014
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 3 15011
Reset M 0 15002 1 15011
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15012
Name     The Hall of Proclamations~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A long hall lined with carved stone tablets stands here, each engraved with
Sith proclamations in the ancient tongue. The tablets tell of conquests,
subjugations, and the names of enemies destroyed. The language is lost to
most but the tone of absolute dominance is unmistakeable even in ignorance.
The altar chamber is to the south and corridors branch east and west.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15011
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15025
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15016
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15017
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 2 15012
Reset M 0 15003 1 15012
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15013
Name     The Eastern Courtyard~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The eastern wing of the outer courtyard holds the ruins of what appears to
have been barracks or training grounds. Stone rings marked with combat sigils
are set into the ground, and the walls bear the scars of a thousand weapon
impacts. The main courtyard is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15014
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15004 2 15013
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15014
Name     The Eastern Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A narrow passage runs between two intact sections of outer wall, connecting
the eastern courtyard to the inner halls. The walls here are covered entirely
in handwritten Sith script, layer upon layer, as though generations of
acolytes practiced their runes here. The south leads to the training grounds
and the west connects to the hall of proclamations.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15011
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15018
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 1 15014
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15015
Name     The Western Courtyard~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The western wing of the courtyard was once a garden of some kind. Dead trees
of twisted black wood still stand at intervals, their trunks carved with Sith
runes from root to branch. The soil beneath them has turned to something more
like ash. Whatever lived here before the dark side took hold is long gone.
The main courtyard lies to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15017
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 2 15015
Reset M 0 15004 1 15015
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15016
Name     The Repository of Names~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This small chamber holds thousands of names carved into the stone walls from
floor to ceiling. These are not the names of the Sith themselves but of their
victims — enemies, rivals, and slaves. The sheer number is staggering. A faint
sense of residual suffering clings to the air here. The hall of proclamations
is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15016
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15017
Name     The Western Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A vaulted passage leads between the outer courts and the inner halls to the
north. Cracked mosaic tiles on the floor depict scenes of conquest. Most are
too damaged to make out clearly but enough remain to paint a picture of
absolute cruelty carried out with artistic pride. The dead garden lies to the
south and the hall of proclamations is to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15019
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15001 1 15017
Reset M 0 15003 1 15017
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15018
Name     The Guard Station~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A fortified guard station controls access to the inner sanctum from the
eastern approach. Murder holes in the ceiling and heavy iron brackets for
barricades suggest this was a serious defensive position. A heavy door to
the north is sealed with Sith rune-locks. The passage behind leads south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15014
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15026
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door iron~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15018
Reset D 0 15018 0 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15019
Name     The Western Guard Station~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The western approach to the inner sanctum is controlled here. Unlike the
eastern station this one has partially collapsed, leaving a gap in the
ceiling through which pale light filters. The defensive works are still
mostly intact however and the passage north is sealed with a rune-locked
door. The western passage is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15017
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15027
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door stone~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15019
Reset D 0 15019 0 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15020
Name     The Courtyard Shrine~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A small shrine stands in a sheltered corner of the outer courtyard. A carved
stone face — some Sith deity or deified lord — stares from a niche in the
wall. Offerings of corroded metal and crumbled bone have been placed before
it. The area around the shrine is conspicuously clear of debris as though
something tends to it still. The main courtyard is accessible to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15020
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15021
Name     The Collapsed Barracks~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The roof of these barracks has partially caved in, admitting grey light and
a cold draft. Stone bunk frames line the walls, long since stripped of
anything useful. A collapsed section of floor near the north wall leads down
to a darkness that smells of age and sealed air — the catacombs are
accessible below though the drop is steep.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15013
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15004 2 15021
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15022
Name     The Weapons Cache~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A hidden alcove behind a false wall in the eastern courtyard area, this cache
was sealed for a very long time. The mechanism that opened it is now jammed
permanently in the open position. Rusted weapon racks and empty containers
fill the space. Most of the contents have long since crumbled to nothing but
a few items appear to have survived through some dark side preservation.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15013
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 15001 1 15022
Reset O 0 15005 1 15022
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15023
Name     The Meditation Circle~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A perfect circle of black stone set into the courtyard floor, ringed with
faded runes of focus and amplification. Standing within it one can feel the
dark side energy of the ruins converging toward this point. The intent was
for Sith to meditate here and draw on the accumulated power of the place.
The feeling of being watched is overwhelming. The courtyard lies to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 1 15023
Reset M 0 15000 2 15023
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15024
Name     The Outer Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A heavy-walled chamber at the edge of the outer courtyard, sealed with
multiple layers of rune-locks that have since been broken from the outside.
The vault has been ransacked at some point in the distant past — drawers
hang open and stone cases are shattered. Whatever was stored here was taken
long ago. The courtyard lies to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 1 15024
Reset O 0 15004 1 15024
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     15025
Name     The Sanctum Threshold~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The boundary between the outer ruins and the inner sanctum is marked by a
massive carved arch, still intact. Sith faces carved into the keystone seem
to track movement with their stone eyes. Passing through it you feel a
palpable increase in the density of dark side energy — heavier, more
purposeful. The outer halls lie to the south and corridors branch north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15028
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15026
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15027
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15025
Reset M 0 15003 1 15025
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15026
Name     The Hall of the Eastern Rite~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The eastern hall of the inner sanctum was dedicated to a specific Sith
ritual whose purpose has been lost. The floor is divided into sections by
carved channels, as though to direct the flow of something. Alcoves line
the walls at regular intervals, each containing the remnants of ceremonial
objects reduced to dust and corroded metal. A sealed door leads south.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15025
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15029
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15018
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door iron~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15026
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15027
Name     The Hall of the Western Rite~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A counterpart to the eastern ritual hall, this chamber served the opposing
half of an ancient ceremony. The geometry of the carvings here is subtly
different — more aggressive, more direct. Where the eastern hall speaks of
preparation this one speaks of execution. A sealed door leads south.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15025
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15030
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15019
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door stone~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15027
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15028
Name     The Chamber of Reflection~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A perfectly square chamber lined with polished black stone that acts as
mirror. Every surface reflects and the effect of infinite reflections
retreating in all directions is deeply unsettling. The Sith used this
chamber for confronting the self and discarding weakness. The threshold is
to the south and corridors branch east, west, and north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15025
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15029
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15030
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15028
Reset M 0 15003 1 15028
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15029
Name     The Eastern Inner Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A long corridor running the eastern length of the inner sanctum. The walls
here have been carved with detailed scenes of Sith history in what must have
been a monumental undertaking. Battle scenes, ritual scenes, and portraits of
Sith lords long forgotten march along the walls in bas-relief. The carving
quality is extraordinarily high.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15028
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15026
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15032
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15029
Reset M 0 15005 1 15029
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15030
Name     The Western Inner Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A long corridor running the western length of the inner sanctum. Less
well-preserved than its eastern counterpart, large sections of the carved
walls have collapsed. What remains shows scenes of subjugation and control —
Sith lords directing vast armies of slaves and lesser beings like pieces
on a game board.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15028
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15027
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15030
Reset M 0 15005 1 15030
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15031
Name     The Hall of Dominion~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The largest room in the inner sanctum, once used for major assemblies and
declarations of Sith supremacy. A raised dais at the northern end still holds
the shattered remains of a great throne. The floor is inlaid with dark
crystal in a star pattern and the ceiling, miraculously intact, soars far
overhead. The chamber still carries the resonance of a thousand declarations
of absolute power.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15028
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15034
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15032
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 3 15031
Reset M 0 15003 2 15031
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15032
Name     The Scriptorium~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Row upon row of stone shelving lines this chamber, each once holding Sith
texts. Most have crumbled to nothing but a few stone tablets survive. The
script on them is the ancient Sith tongue but even without translation the
diagrams that accompany the text make their subject matter clear: weapons,
poisons, and methods of control. The corridor is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15029
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15032
Reset O 0 15004 1 15032
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15033
Name     The Alchemy Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This chamber was used for Sith alchemy — the dark side art of corrupting
and reshaping living things and materials. Stone tables with corroded metal
fittings fill the room and arcane distillation equipment lies shattered on
the floor. Faint discolouration on the walls and ceiling suggests that things
have happened here that cannot be easily described.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15030
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15033
Reset O 0 15003 1 15033
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15034
Name     The Approach to the Deep Sanctum~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The northern end of the inner sanctum narrows to a single grand corridor
that leads toward the deep sanctum. The architecture here becomes more
extreme — the walls lean slightly inward, the ceiling lowers, and the carvings
become more intense and urgent. Whatever the Sith considered most sacred lay
ahead and they designed the approach to convey that. The hall of dominion
is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15035
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15036
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15034
Reset M 0 15003 1 15034
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15035
Name     The Gate of Inner Darkness~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A pair of massive stone doors stands here, each carved with the face of a
different Sith entity. The doors are sealed with a Sith lock that requires
specific knowledge to bypass. The ancient mechanisms still function though
they have clearly been forced open and re-sealed multiple times over the
centuries. Beyond lies the deep sanctum. The approach corridor lies south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15034
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15050
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door stone rune~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 3 15035
Reset D 0 15035 0 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15036
Name     The Inner Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A side chamber off the main approach, this archive contains records carved
into the walls themselves — an encyclopedia of Sith knowledge that spans
the full height of the room. Most of the content is beyond interpretation
without a deep knowledge of the ancient language but a few sections contain
diagrams clear enough to understand. The approach corridor is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15034
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15037
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 3 15036
Reset O 0 15004 1 15036
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15037
Name     The Relic Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A small heavily protected chamber that once held important Sith relics.
Most of its contents have been taken or destroyed over the centuries but
the protective wards that remain are still active — you feel them probing
at your presence as you enter. A few items may still be found here if one
searches carefully. The archive is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15036
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15037
Reset O 0 15000 1 15037
Reset O 0 15006 1 15037
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15038
Name     The Corridor of Penitence~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A long narrow corridor whose walls are lined with iron fixtures that once
held restraints. This was the path taken by those who had displeased the
ruling Sith and were being brought to judgment. The floor is worn smooth
by countless feet. The meaning of the carvings above the restraint fixtures
is mercifully unclear. The sanctum threshold area connects to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15025
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15039
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15038
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15039
Name     The Judgment Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A high-ceilinged chamber with a single elevated seat at the far end. This
was where Sith lords passed judgment on those brought through the corridor of
penitence. The stone floor below the seat is deeply stained and the drainage
channels carved into it tell a grim story. The corridor of penitence leads
south and stairs descend to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15038
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15040
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15039
Reset M 0 15003 1 15039
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15040
Name     The Descent to the Catacombs~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A broad staircase carved directly into the bedrock descends from the inner
sanctum into the catacombs below. Cold air rises from below carrying the
smell of stone dust and something organic and old. Wall torches that once
lined the stair have long since burned out. The judgment hall is to the west
and the catacombs lie below to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15039
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15050
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 1 15040
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     15041
Name     The Chamber of Whispers~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A domed chamber with unusual acoustics — sound behaves strangely here,
voices doubling and tripling unexpectedly. The Sith used this chamber for
interrogation, as the disorienting acoustics could reduce subjects to
confession within minutes. The chamber connects east to the inner halls.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15041
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15042
Name     The Antechamber of the Throne~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Directly before the shattered throne room, this antechamber served as a
waiting area for those granted an audience. The stone benches are worn smooth
with use. The carvings here depict the rewards of loyalty in considerable
detail — power, wealth, and the subjugation of enemies. The hall of dominion
lies to the south and the throne approach is north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15042
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15043
Name     The Shattered Throne Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The throne itself is broken, split down the middle by some ancient and
powerful impact. The chamber around it shows signs of a tremendous battle —
scorch marks on the walls, deep gouges in the stone, entire sections of
carved relief blasted away. Whatever conflict ended the power of Kar'ethis
reached its climax here. Shards of the black throne litter the floor. The
antechamber lies south and hidden passages may yet exist.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15042
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15044
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15043
Reset M 0 15003 2 15043
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15044
Name     The Private Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A concealed vault directly adjacent to the throne room, accessible through
a hidden door that has long since been found. This was where the ruling Sith
lord kept personal treasures and items too dangerous to store elsewhere.
The vault has been picked over many times but its warding enchantments may
have preserved some items against those who lacked the knowledge to safely
remove them. The throne room is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 1 15044
Reset O 0 15000 1 15044
Reset O 0 15002 1 15044
Reset O 0 15003 1 15044
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15045
Name     The Armoury of the Guard~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The personal armoury of the Sith lord's guard detachment lies here, its
heavy door still hanging on intact hinges. The weapon racks and armour
stands are largely empty but some pieces survived the intervening centuries
through dark side preservation. The chamber connects to the inner halls.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15045
Reset O 0 15001 1 15045
Reset O 0 15005 1 15045
Reset O 0 15006 1 15045
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15046
Name     The Garden of Death~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     An internal courtyard open to the dead sky above, this was the Sith lord's
private garden. Every plant that once grew here has long since died and
turned to dust and black residue. The garden paths are still clearly marked
by their edging stones. At the centre is a dry fountain carved in the shape
of a coiled serpentine creature. Passages lead in multiple directions.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15045
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15004 3 15046
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15047
Name     The Observatory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A tall tower chamber with a domed ceiling that has collapsed inward, opening
to the sky. Elaborate astronomical instruments of corroded metal fill the room.
The Sith used celestial observation to time their rituals. Markings on the
floor show complex alignment calculations. From here the full sweep of the
ruins is visible when looking up through the collapsed dome.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15034
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 2 15047
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15048
Name     The Laboratory of Dark Experiments~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A chamber that defies easy description. The equipment here served purposes
that the casual observer cannot easily categorise. Stone tables with complex
restraint mechanisms. Glass vessels of unusual shapes. Channels cut into
the floors at precise angles. Whatever research was conducted here pushed
far beyond conventional bounds. The smell that clings to the walls is
organic and wrong. The deep sanctum approach lies north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15035
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15048
Reset M 0 15003 1 15048
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15049
Name     The Corridor of the Fallen~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A corridor lined with niches, each containing the standing remains of a
Sith warrior in full armour. Whether these are ceremonially interred dead or
simply empty suits of armour placed here as honour guard it is impossible to
tell. The armour is extraordinary — ancient Sith battle plate of a design
not seen for millennia. All of it is corroded beyond use. The corridor
connects the inner sanctum areas.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15031
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15035
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15049
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     15050
Name     The Upper Catacombs~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     You descend into the catacombs of Kar'ethis. The air is cold, dry, and
completely still. Niches carved into the walls hold the remains of those
who served the Sith in life and were interred here in death. The scale is
immense — the catacombs extend far deeper than the ruins above would suggest.
The gate of inner darkness is above to the south and the staircase descent
is also accessible. Passages branch deeper.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15035
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door stone rune~
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15051
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15052
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15053
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    15040
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 3 15050
Reset M 0 15000 2 15050
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15051
Name     The Hall of the Interred~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The primary hall of the upper catacombs extends north in a long straight
line. The density of interred remains increases here — three rows of niches
on each side, floor to ceiling. Thousands of individuals are buried here,
each with a small carved tablet bearing their name and their service record.
The dark side energy is palpable and oppressive.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15050
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15054
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15055
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15051
Reset M 0 15005 2 15051
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15052
Name     The Eastern Catacomb Branch~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The eastern branch of the upper catacombs is older than the main hall —
the carving style is different and the niches are arranged differently.
This section predates the main Kar'ethis settlement and may have been an
existing structure that the later Sith incorporated into their complex.
The main entrance is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15050
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15056
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15052
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15053
Name     The Western Catacomb Branch~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The western branch contains the most recent interments in the catacombs.
Unlike the orderly niches of the main hall these have been carved with
less care and the tablets are cruder. The wraiths that drift through
this section seem more agitated than elsewhere, as though the more
recent dead have not fully accepted their situation. The entrance is east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15050
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15057
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 3 15053
Reset M 0 15000 2 15053
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15054
Name     The Ritual Burial Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A large chamber devoted to the burial rites of high-ranking Sith. The
preparations for interment were elaborate and the equipment used is still
present — stone implements for preservation, frames for positioning the
remains, and tables covered in ritual tools. The carvings here depict
the Sith afterlife concept in considerable detail. A dark and determined
view of what follows death.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15051
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15058
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15057
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15054
Reset M 0 15005 2 15054
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15055
Name     The Chamber of Preserved Lords~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A sealed inner chamber that once required specific ritual knowledge to
enter. The seals have been broken at some point. Inside are the preserved
remains of what appear to be high-ranking Sith lords, each in an elaborate
stone sarcophagus carved in their likeness. The preservation is unsettlingly
effective — the remains appear almost alive in the low dark side light.
The hall of the interred is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15051
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 3 15055
Reset M 0 15000 2 15055
Reset O 0 15000 1 15055
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15056
Name     The Ancient Catacombs~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The oldest section of the Kar'ethis catacombs, predating the Sith by a
significant margin. Whoever built this section used a different style and
a different purpose. The niches here are empty but the carvings are neither
Sith nor any recognisable tradition. Geometric patterns and unidentified
symbols. The eastern branch of newer catacombs is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15052
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15059
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15056
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15057
Name     The Flooded Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     This passage has been partially flooded by water seeping through the bedrock
over centuries. Black water — unnaturally still — covers the floor to knee
depth. Narrow ledges along the walls allow passage without wading but they
are uneven. The water is cold beyond reason and something moves in it that
is better not examined closely. Passages connect south and east.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15053
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15054
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15060
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15057
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15058
Name     The Deep Ritual Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     Below the ritual burial chamber lies this deeper space used for ceremonies
that the Sith preferred to conduct in absolute darkness and isolation.
The walls are covered in densely layered runes of a complexity that suggests
years of continuous addition. The dark side energy here is intense enough
to cause a slight physical pressure. The burial chamber is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15054
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15061
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15062
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15058
Reset M 0 15005 2 15058
Reset M 0 15003 1 15058
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15059
Name     The Void Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The ancient builders constructed this chamber for a purpose unknown. A
perfectly spherical room with smooth walls, a flat floor, and no visible
means of support for the ceiling. No carvings. No niches. No purpose that
can be determined by observation. The Sith left it exactly as they found
it, which says something. The ancient catacombs lie to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15056
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 1 15059
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15060
Name     The Drowned Gallery~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The flooding here is more severe than in the passage below. Carved panels
that once depicted significant events in Sith history are submerged to
their upper thirds, the images preserved below the waterline in perfect
detail. What can be seen above the black water tells a story of rise to
power that remains compelling even now. Passages lead south and east.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15057
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15061
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15063
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15060
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15061
Name     The Chamber of the Marked~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     This chamber held Sith who had been marked for eventual execution — kept
alive for purposes of information or forced service before their inevitable
end. Heavy iron fixtures remain in the walls and the stone is worn in
patterns that suggest long-term occupation under restraint. The dark side
energy here has a specific flavour — resignation layered over hatred.
Passages lead west, south, and north.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15060
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15058
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15064
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15061
Reset M 0 15005 2 15061
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15062
Name     The Repository of Curses~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A chamber sealed with seventeen layers of warding when it was first built.
Fifteen of those wards remain active. The two that failed did so within the
first century. The repository holds inscribed tablets bearing Sith curses of
the highest order — compendiums of dark knowledge meant to empower the
curses laid upon enemies. The content is genuinely dangerous even to read.
The deep ritual chamber lies to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15058
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 3 15062
Reset O 0 15004 1 15062
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15063
Name     The Underground Reservoir~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     An underground reservoir fed by natural springs, the water here is the
source of the flooding in the catacombs below. The Sith used this water
in rituals — it has absorbed centuries of dark side energy and has
properties that cannot be described as entirely natural. The reservoir is
ringed by a stone walkway and descends to a depth not easily determined.
The drowned gallery is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15060
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15064
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15063
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15064
Name     The Descent to the Throne Catacombs~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The deepest accessible point of the catacombs opens onto a stairway leading
further down toward the areas beneath the throne chamber. The construction
here is the most deliberate of any in the catacombs — every stone placed
with specific intent. Whatever lies below was meant to be permanent and
meant to be found only by those with the knowledge and strength to reach it.
Passages lead north, west, and south.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15063
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15061
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15064
Reset M 0 15005 1 15064
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     15065
Name     The Gallery of Faces~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     One thousand carved faces line this narrow gallery, each distinct. These
are death masks — the faces of Sith recorded at the moment of their death.
The expressions range across a spectrum from absolute fury to something
approaching transcendence. The gallery connects the western catacombs.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15053
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15066
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 2 15065
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15066
Name     The Chamber of Silence~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark silence~
Desc     A chamber in which no sound functions — not speech, not footsteps, nothing.
The silence here is not natural but enforced by Sith sorcery that persists
millennia after its creators died. Communication here requires other means.
The isolation is deeply uncomfortable. The gallery of faces lies to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15065
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15066
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15067
Name     The Lower Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A secondary archive in the catacombs holds records of the dead — not just
names but detailed accounts of service, failure, and the punishments meted
out for that failure. The Sith kept exceptionally detailed records. The
lower archive connects to the hall of the interred above.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    15051
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15068
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15067
Reset O 0 15004 1 15067
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15068
Name     The Sarcophagus Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A hall of ornate sarcophagi, each sealed with heavy stone lids carved in
elaborate detail. The sarcophagi are arranged in a formal pattern that
mirrors the constellation charts found in the observatory above. The dark
side energy here has a focused quality, directed inward toward each
sarcophagus as though something within each one is still active.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15067
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15054
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15068
Reset M 0 15005 2 15068
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15069
Name     The Black Pool~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A perfectly still pool of black liquid that predates the Sith occupation
of these ruins. The Sith built around it and incorporated it into their
rituals without fully understanding what it was. The surface of the pool
reflects nothing. Objects lowered into it vanish. The pool connects to the
deeper catacombs.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15054
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15070
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 3 15069
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15070
Name     The Stone Forest~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     Hundreds of stone pillars of varying heights fill this chamber in a pattern
that suggests a forest. Moving through them requires care. The pillars are
carved to appear as twisted trees and the effect in darkness is deeply
unsettling. The dark side has given some of the carved branches an
appearance of movement. The black pool is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15069
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15058
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 4 15070
Reset M 0 15005 3 15070
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15071
Name     The Passage of Last Rites~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The formal processional route used when interring high-ranking Sith. The
floor is polished black stone, still maintained by something — the dust that
fills every other corridor of the catacombs does not accumulate here.
The passage connects the ritual areas to the deeper sections.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15054
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15072
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 2 15071
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15072
Name     The Hall of Echoes~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     This chamber has unusual properties — sounds made here are recorded and
played back at irregular intervals. Voices speaking in the ancient tongue,
rhythmic chanting, and occasionally what sounds like screaming in multiple
registers have been heard here. The Sith found this useful. The passage
of last rites leads north and the catacombs extend east.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15071
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15073
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15072
Reset M 0 15000 2 15072
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15073
Name     The Convergence Point~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     Dark side energy lines running through the bedrock of the ruins converge
here at a point marked by a single carved pillar of black stone. Standing
near it, the dark side pressure is stronger than anywhere else in the
catacombs. Force users feel it as a constant pull. The hall of echoes is
to the west and the deeper catacombs extend north.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15072
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15063
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15073
Reset M 0 15005 2 15073
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15074
Name     The Hidden Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A concealed passage that bypasses the more heavily trafficked catacomb
routes. It is narrow, requiring movement in single file, and runs in a
diagonal that connects two distant parts of the catacomb system. The walls
here are uncarved — this was a functional route, not a ceremonial one.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15064
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15058
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 1 15074
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     15075
Name     The Antechamber of Power~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The deepest level of the ruins opens into an antechamber of extraordinary
construction. Every surface has been worked with a precision that surpasses
anything above. The stone itself seems different — darker, denser, as though
it was sourced from somewhere other than the local bedrock. The dark side
energy here is almost physically tangible. Stairs lead back up to the
catacombs to the south. The way forward leads north toward the heart of
Kar'ethis.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15064
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15076
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15077
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15078
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 3 15075
Reset M 0 15003 2 15075
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15076
Name     The Gallery of the Fallen Lords~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     Massive stone portraits — each several metres tall — line this gallery,
depicting the lords of Kar'ethis in order of succession. Their expressions
convey absolute certainty in their own power and absolute contempt for
everything else. The final portrait in the sequence has been deliberately
defaced, the face gouged away by something with considerable force. The
antechamber is to the south and the path continues north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15079
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15076
Reset M 0 15005 2 15076
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15077
Name     The Eastern Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A vault sealed with the most complex rune-lock mechanisms in the entire
ruins. The locks have been opened — whether by those with genuine knowledge
or by brute force is unclear. The interior shows signs of both methodical
removal and violent ransacking at different points in its history. Some
items remain, preserved by wards that are still active. The antechamber
lies to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15077
Reset O 0 15000 1 15077
Reset O 0 15002 1 15077
Reset O 0 15005 1 15077
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15078
Name     The Western Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The western vault appears to have been sealed more recently than its eastern
counterpart — the mechanisms are different and the rune-locks show a more
advanced technique. The interior is less disturbed. Whatever was placed here
was added after the main occupation of the ruins ended. The antechamber is
to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15078
Reset O 0 15001 1 15078
Reset O 0 15003 1 15078
Reset O 0 15006 1 15078
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15079
Name     The Corridor of Final Warning~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The corridor before the throne chamber is the densest collection of warning
inscriptions in the ruins. In the ancient Sith tongue, in several other dead
languages, and — notably — in Basic, a single message is repeated hundreds
of times in varying sizes: TURN BACK. The sheer repetition suggests that
the Sith who placed this warning were themselves afraid of what lay beyond.
The gallery is to the south and the throne chamber door lies north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15076
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15080
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door obsidian seal~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15079
Reset M 0 15003 2 15079
Reset D 0 15079 0 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15080
Name     The Throne Chamber of Kar'ethis~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The throne chamber is vast — far larger than the external dimensions of the
ruins should permit. A ceiling that disappears into darkness. Walls carved
with every significant event in the history of Kar'ethis in extraordinary
detail. At the far end, on a raised dais of black stone that rises in seven
steps, sits the Throne of Kar'ethis — intact, unlike the shattered one above.

The dark side energy here is beyond description. It has weight, direction,
and intent. It presses inward from all sides and from the floor beneath your
feet and from the Throne itself, which radiates it in concentrated waves.

And the Lord of Kar'ethis waits here. It has waited a very long time. It
regards you with the cold certainty that you were always going to come here
and that this was always going to end one way. The corridor of warning lies
to the south and sealed passages branch east and west.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15079
Flags     isdoor closed~
Keywords  door obsidian seal~
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15081
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15082
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15083
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15006 1 15080
Reset D 0 15080 2 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15081
Name     The Eastern Sanctum Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     Behind the throne, to the east, a vault of the most significant items
the Lord of Kar'ethis possessed in life. The dark side energy preserves
everything within perfectly. The items here are extraordinary by any
measure — instruments of power accumulated over centuries of rule. The
throne chamber lies to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15080
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 15000 1 15081
Reset O 0 15001 1 15081
Reset O 0 15002 1 15081
Reset O 0 15003 1 15081
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15082
Name     The Western Sanctum Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The western vault behind the throne holds items of a different category —
knowledge rather than power. Tablets, inscribed stones, and sealed containers
whose contents defy easy categorisation. The Lord of Kar'ethis considered
knowledge and power as equivalent things, and this collection reflects that
philosophy. The throne chamber lies to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15080
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 15004 1 15082
Reset O 0 15000 1 15082
Reset O 0 15006 1 15082
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15083
Name     The Chamber Behind the Throne~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The chamber directly behind the throne is the most private space in all of
Kar'ethis. Only the Lord of Kar'ethis entered here. The contents are
minimalist compared to the ostentatious display of power elsewhere — a single
stone table, a stone chair, and walls covered in personal inscriptions written
in a compressed private shorthand. Whatever the Lord of Kar'ethis was when
alone, it was not the same as the mask worn in public. The throne chamber
lies to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15080
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15084
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 2 15083
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15084
Name     The Memory Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The innermost accessible room of the ruins, a small chamber where the Lord
of Kar'ethis stored items of personal significance. Unlike the vaults these
were not catalogued or organised. The contents are scattered with what might
be called personality — mementos, favoured objects, things kept for reasons
known only to their owner. The dark side presence here is quieter than
elsewhere. Almost contemplative. The private chamber is to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15083
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 15004 1 15084
Reset O 0 15000 1 15084
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     15085
Name     The Hall of Tribute~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A formal hall where tribute from conquered worlds and subjugated peoples was
brought and catalogued before being distributed. The records of tribute are
inscribed on the walls in exhaustive detail — quantities, dates, the names
of those who delivered it and the names of those who accepted on behalf of
Kar'ethis. The scale of the operation documented here is staggering.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15076
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15077
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15085
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15086
Name     The Guard Barracks of the Deep~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The deepest barracks in the ruins, used by the Lord's personal guard who
never left this level. The accommodations are Spartan but the guard served
willingly — being this close to the seat of power was its own reward in
Sith culture. The furnishings are long since rotted but the structure
is perfectly intact. Corridors lead to the antechamber.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 3 15086
Reset O 0 15005 1 15086
Reset O 0 15006 1 15086
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15087
Name     The Command Post~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A heavily reinforced command post from which the Lord of Kar'ethis could
direct the defence of the ruins in the event of attack. Maps — carved stone
relief maps of the surrounding region — still cover one entire wall. The
tactical detail is extraordinary. Communication equipment of an archaic design
lines another wall. The antechamber lies to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15087
Reset M 0 15002 2 15087
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15088
Name     The Trophy Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The Lord of Kar'ethis kept trophies. The hall extends for a considerable
distance and every available surface holds mounted items from conquered
enemies and defeated rivals. Weapons, armour, insignia, and items of more
personal significance are all represented. The collection covers centuries.
Each trophy has a small inscription beneath it identifying the previous owner
and noting the circumstances under which it was taken.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15080
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 2 15088
Reset O 0 15001 1 15088
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15089
Name     The Sanctum Passage North~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A straight corridor connecting the northernmost reaches of the deep sanctum
to the throne chamber area. The walls here are plain — no carvings, no
inscriptions, no decorative elements. This was a functional passage built for
speed of movement rather than impression. The throne area lies to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15080
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15090
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15002 2 15089
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15090
Name     The Sealed Sanctum~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A sanctum that was sealed after the fall of Kar'ethis and remained
sealed for millennia. The seals failed slowly over time. The interior is in
extraordinary condition as a result of the prolonged sealing — dust, decay,
and disturbance have all been held back. The contents are exactly as they
were left. The corridor lies to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15089
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 3 15090
Reset O 0 15000 1 15090
Reset O 0 15002 1 15090
Reset O 0 15004 1 15090
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15091
Name     The Lower Archives~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A final set of archives at the deepest level, holding the most sensitive
and dangerous records of the Kar'ethis Sith. Access to these archives was
restricted to the Lord and two designated archivists. The content covers
topics that would be considered unacceptable in any other context. The
antechamber area connects to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15092
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15091
Reset O 0 15004 1 15091
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15092
Name     The Laboratory of the Lord~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The private laboratory of the Lord of Kar'ethis, where personal research
was conducted in absolute secrecy. The equipment here is of a significantly
higher calibre than the alchemy chamber above. Whatever was studied here was
done so with exceptional resources and exceptional expertise. The notes that
remain are in the compressed private shorthand seen in the private chamber —
without the key they are unreadable. The archives are to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15091
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15092
Reset O 0 15004 1 15092
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15093
Name     The Power Nexus~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     At the geometric centre of the deep sanctum lies the power nexus — the
point around which the entire structure of Kar'ethis was built. A column of
black stone rises from floor to ceiling, its surface covered entirely in
runes that pulse faintly with residual dark side energy. The nexus is the
source and sustainer of everything that makes these ruins what they are.
Passages connect to the throne area.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15075
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 4 15093
Reset M 0 15005 3 15093
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15094
Name     The Chamber of Legacies~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A chamber dedicated to recording and preserving the legacies of the lords
of Kar'ethis for all time. Each lord has a dedicated alcove with a full
accounting of their rule, achievements, and end. The most recent alcove —
for the final lord — has only half its panels completed. The account ends
abruptly mid-sentence, as though the archivist was interrupted and never
returned. The throne chamber area connects to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15076
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 1 15094
Reset M 0 15000 2 15094
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15095
Name     The Consecrated Ground~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A section of the deep sanctum that was consecrated to the dark side with
a thoroughness beyond that of the rest of the ruins. Standing here, even
those without Force sensitivity can feel something pressing at the edges of
their perception. For those with Force ability, the experience is considerably
more intense. The sanctum passages connect here.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15079
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    15093
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 3 15095
Reset M 0 15005 2 15095
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15096
Name     The Circle of Binding~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A circular chamber whose floor is a single continuous binding rune of
extraordinary complexity. The rune has been in continuous effect since it
was first inscribed. Several entities have been bound here over the centuries.
Some are still bound. The chamber connects to the deep sanctum.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    15093
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 4 15096
Reset M 0 15000 3 15096
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15097
Name     The Passage of Absolute Dark~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A passage in which no light of any kind functions — not natural light, not
technological light, and not the light produced by Force abilities. Navigation
here is by memory and touch. The darkness is complete and the sounds within
it are best not analysed too carefully. The passage connects deep areas.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15080
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15093
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15005 2 15097
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15098
Name     The Terminus~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The furthest point of the accessible ruins — a chamber that appears to
continue beyond its visible walls into darkness that swallows all illumination.
The feeling here is of standing at an edge beyond which different rules apply.
Whatever the Sith built beyond this point was either destroyed or remains
inaccessible. The deep sanctum connects to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    15097
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15000 2 15098
Reset M 0 15005 2 15098
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     15099
Name     The Outer Reliquary~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A reliquary positioned at the outer edge of the throne chamber complex,
serving as a last repository of significant items before the sanctum proper.
The reliquary is better preserved than the main vaults, its warding still
substantially intact. The items within may be among the most significant
remaining in the ruins. The throne chamber area connects to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    15080
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 15003 2 15099
Reset O 0 15000 1 15099
Reset O 0 15001 1 15099
Reset O 0 15002 1 15099
Reset O 0 15003 1 15099
Reset O 0 15005 1 15099
